+Subject: [PATCH 6/6] feat(guardian): Fase 6 Tahap 1 -- Guardian Orchestrator
+ wires all 13 modules
+
+Closes known_issues.md #11 (sentinel.py only wired 5/13 modules).
+
+New yomi_core/guardian.py: GuardianOrchestrator, the single place that
+decides which deep-dive modules fire in response to a triage outcome,
+gated entirely by yomi_core.module_registry (never ad-hoc env vars).
+
+- handle_post_containment(pid): dispatches MIND_READER, REMEDIATOR,
+  SANDBOX, MIRAGE after a SYNCHRONOUS containment success (instant
+  CRITICAL SIGSTOP, or harness SUCCESS/FROZEN). Deliberately does NOT
+  chain these off Shadow Net escalation (async, fire-and-forget --
+  outcome unknown at call time, would be a race condition).
+- handle_escalation(pid, reason): fire-and-forget dispatches SHADOW_NET
+  on ESCALATED_TO_SHADOW_NET.
+- generate_incident_dossier(): unconditional at end of every incident
+  if DOSSIER enabled.
+- periodic_maintenance(): sweeps orphaned MIRAGE decoys every 20 cycles.
+- bootstrap_startup_daemons(): wires GHOST + EBPF_SENSOR at CLI startup.
+
+Every dispatch try/except-guarded and logged to ledger on failure
+(<MODULE>_DISPATCH_ERROR), never raised -- one module failing can't
+take down the observation loop.
+
+Wired into sentinel.py (_zero_prompt_trigger, 3 dispatch points) and
+cli.py (bootstrap_startup_daemons replaces two ad-hoc call sites).
+
+Also fixes known_issues.md #26: Ghost Protocol was gated by
+YOMI_ENABLE_GHOST_PROTOCOL (never module_registry's YOMI_MODULE_GHOST);
+the eBPF Sensor had NO gating at all -- cli.py unconditionally spawned
+it regardless of EBPF_SENSOR's default_enabled=False. Both now go
+through module_registry exclusively. BREAKING: YOMI_ENABLE_GHOST_PROTOCOL
+-> YOMI_MODULE_GHOST.
+
+Documents known_issues.md #25 (mirage.py's own YOMI_ENABLE_MIRAGE_MODE
+env var vs module_registry's YOMI_MODULE_MIRAGE -- worked around via
+force_enable=True, not removed, to avoid breaking existing
+test_mirage.py assertions).
+
+Tests: tests/unit/test_guardian.py (25 new tests, 93% coverage of
+guardian.py). tests/integration/test_chain_sentinel_router_harness.py
+fixture fixed to isolate remediator/dossier/library __file__ paths too
+(previously only swarm.py was isolated -- guardian's new dispatch was
+writing REAL dossier PDFs into the actual repo's yomi_data/reports/
+before this fix, caught by manually diffing git status after a green
+test run, not by trusting PASSED alone). New assertions there prove
+real dispatch against a real subprocess PID: REMEDIATOR correctly
+refuses the real python3 interpreter path (/usr, per #15's containment
+fix) and DOSSIER generates a real signed report.
+
+Found and fixed 2 of my own test bugs: two test_guardian.py tests
+constructed GuardianOrchestrator() manually without requesting the
+isolated_stamp fixture, leaking into the real ImmutableStamp singleton.
+Caught by scanning every test individually and diffing yomi_data/ after
+each, not by assuming green tests meant no side effects.
+
+Verified: 483/483 total (477 unit + 5 integration + 1 benchmark)
+passed as root. 5x stable as non-root. Lint clean. git status clean
+after every test run (no leaked files in yomi_data/).
+
+Both feature/guardian-orchestrator and feature/module-registry branches
+were verified byte-identical to develop for module_registry.py and
+sentinel.py before starting -- no hidden prior work to merge from them.
+
+Explicitly NOT touched: known_issues.md #9 (ImmutableStamp singleton /
+multi-tenant architecture) remains a separate, deferred decision.
